Instruction version: 1

Source PR: https://github.com/trinitron88/earworm/pull/10
Reviewed publication: `60ff5b4dc116c989dcf4f904577fe7cfc54706ca`
Confirmed merge / exact next base: `199143f6c590cda68f1acfc1829adcabf0d57ae8`
Review: https://github.com/trinitron88/earworm/pull/10#pullrequestreview-5259857321
Actual held-out execution revision: `dd4fbea06485bd00117e9340a83a8844859869c5`

PR #10 is accepted as branch A for its bounded supplied-boundary task. Saved-output review verified all 80 checksums, 8,352 hash-chain records, 6,048 independently reconstructed forecasts/scores within `2.22e-16`, 96 future-invariance probes and 277 preserved historical artifacts. The repaired adapter plus unchanged PR #8 reference reached 48/48 in all four cells, versus old-observation 36/48 under timbre/joint change; joint gain `.25`, paired 95% interval `[.083333,.416667]`. All adoption, causal and octave-safety gates passed. This does not establish segmentation, natural-music performance, polyphony, perceptual identity or relational superiority.

Authorization: delegated in-plan implementation AND execution under continuous 24/7 PM authority in comments 5747905320 and 5747969943. This is the single next assignment. Reconcile the completion receipt 5748288820, processed instruction IDs and no-overlap lock before starting; reuse matching work/PR if present and never dispatch a duplicate.

Decision: can the selected repaired observation plus simple retrieval operate on a causal continuous monophonic voice without evaluator-supplied note boundaries, closely enough to advance to controlled isolated-voice motif transformations?
Result A → if the causal streaming front end passes the preregistered prediction, boundary, noninferiority, causal-control and safety gates, retain it as a versioned front end and, after review, advance to one bounded controlled isolated-voice transformation/recombination stage.
Result B → if the supplied-boundary ceiling passes but the streaming front end fails and the frozen diagnostics localize the loss to boundary formation, do not advance musical complexity; preserve the evidence and, after review, authorize one targeted segmentation repair on fresh groups.
Result C → if the supplied-boundary ceiling also fails on the fresh continuous-rendering task, do not blame segmentation or retune exposed groups; retain the PR #10 bounded claim and, after review, choose a different controlled readout/task prerequisite within the roadmap.
Inconclusive/invalid → preserve all results and stop. The PM selects a genuinely discriminating in-plan action or checkpoints a concrete blocker; no descriptive audit.
Stop condition: one frozen evaluation, one complete reproducible successor and branch receipt, then stop for exact-head review. No worker self-dispatch of the next stage.

IMPLEMENT AND RUN

Create `experiments/continuous-isolated-voice-v1/` from current main `199143f6c590cda68f1acfc1829adcabf0d57ae8`. Preserve E08, PR #8, PR #9, PR #10 and every historical artifact byte-for-byte. Keep the accepted repaired observation algorithm and the PR #8 relative-retrieval reference parameters frozen for the primary comparison. The only new learned/selected component may be ONE lightweight causal boundary/event-forming front end with a finite development-only configuration. Record every difference. No relational-model objective.

Use a truly continuous monophonic waveform: render each arrived history/probe as one uninterrupted isolated voice, then deliver it only as contiguous fixed-duration PCM chunks whose edges are deliberately not note boundaries. The predictor receives chunk bytes and arrival order only—no note durations, note starts/ends, MIDI/pitch labels, generator metadata, phrase identity, future bytes or whole-waveform features. Boundary decisions may use only arrived samples, with a fixed preregistered causal latency; a note/event is final only after its required arrived evidence exists. Durably fsync the forecast before continuation bytes arrive or are extracted.

Retain the repaired NSDF observation inside inferred completed events, including availability, candidates and uncertainty. Do not silently use the accepted supplied-boundary implementation as the streaming system. Preserve it as an evaluator-separated ceiling comparator given the same arrived waveform and true boundaries after generation; label it `oracle-boundary`, never as an acoustic capability. Include a simple fixed-window/no-event comparator. Give present-only, marginal, recency, transitions orders 1–3, absolute retrieval and transformation-aware retrieval the same operational events/history budget within each front end. Do not intentionally impoverish baselines.

STIMULI AND SPLITS

Use 40 fresh disjoint phrase groups: 8 development, 8 calibration, 24 held out. All paired/control/render variants of a group stay in one split. Use new normalized motif/continuation tuples, seeds and waveform hashes with zero overlap against prior evaluation groups. No Bach excerpt, natural performance or simultaneous voices yet.

Each group must preserve the history-dependent prediction task: paired histories have byte-identical current probes, balanced sound inventories/counts/frequencies/durations/timbre/energy, balanced order and recency, adequate equal memory and zero eviction, but different temporal bindings imply different continuations. Cross pitch direction, register, overtone family, presentation order and articulation independently where the finite design permits; declare aliases before evaluation.

Predefine four operational cells:
1. detached: short audible inter-note gaps, chunk edges offset from boundaries;
2. legato: no silence at pitch transitions;
3. duration-jitter: unseen note durations and transitions offset from chunk edges;
4. joint: legato plus duration jitter and the already-supported controlled timbre/envelope change.
Use fixed contiguous chunks of 40–80 ms selected on development only; at most 32 arrived chunks enter any forecast. Ensure each complete waveform unit is <=2 seconds and disclose total arrived prefix duration. The final current probe waveform must remain byte-identical within each paired history. Do not choose evaluation render parameters after seeing results.

Retain reset, relevant-history removal, swap, whole-motif order shuffle and ambiguous-history controls in the joint cell. Controls must have valid labels and preserve the intended nuisance balance. Test unrevealed-future invariance by substituting withheld continuation bytes without changing the committed forecast.

PREREGISTRATION AND VALIDITY

Before generating or exposing held-out waveforms/results, freeze and post to PR #2 the protocol, implementation/config/split/model hashes; finite boundary parameter grid; chunk length and latency; event matching/tolerances; probability coordinates/calibration; resource ledger; bootstrap seed/quantiles; controls; all branch criteria. Development selects the finite boundary configuration. Calibration performs integrity checks and any explicitly preregistered probability calibration only; no evaluation tuning. One held-out pass, no group replacement, acoustic rerun, post-hoc repaired evaluation or threshold weakening.

Required validity gates:
- fixed split/freshness and factor balance;
- prefix-only worker API/process guard; no future or metadata path;
- append-only hash chain and fsynced pre-reveal forecast;
- same forecast bytes under future substitution;
- exact paired byte/inventory/current-probe balance;
- equal history/capacity and zero eviction;
- exact historical source/config hashes;
- all causal-control semantics;
- all stream/compute/storage caps;
- saved-result reconstruction independent of the operational predictor.

Evaluate equally by phrase group. Report point accuracy, both-members paired success, log loss and Brier for every front end/model/cell/control. Use 5,000 paired phrase-group bootstrap resamples with a fixed preregistered seed and familywise intervals across the four streaming-minus-oracle cell comparisons.

Also report evaluator-only event formation by group: precision, recall/F1, split/merge counts, onset/end error, pitch availability/error and causal decision latency. Truth is scoring-only and must never enter the operational worker.

BRANCH CRITERIA

Validity gates pass first. The oracle-boundary repaired reference must reach paired success >=.80 in every cell; otherwise select C.

Select A only if all of the following hold:
- streaming repaired reference paired success >=.80 in every cell;
- streaming-minus-oracle accuracy lower familywise 95% bound >=-.10 in every cell;
- streaming joint advantage over streaming present-only has positive lower paired 95% bound;
- streaming joint log-loss increase versus oracle <=.10 and Brier increase <=.02, using preregistered paired group summaries;
- group-weighted event F1 >=.90, pitched-event accuracy within .35 semitone >=.95, split rate <=.05 and merge rate <=.05;
- causal decision latency stays within the frozen arrived-audio bound;
- reset/removal paired success <=.10 and accuracy <=.55 with paired forecast TV <=1e-9; swap counterpart probability error <=1e-9 and paired success >=.80; information-preserving shuffle accuracy drop <=.10; ambiguous alternatives total mass >=.90, each within .10 of .5 and max class probability <=.60;
- no prerecorded safety subfamily loses more than .10 group-mean accuracy versus oracle boundary, and octave-error rate remains <=1%.

Select B when oracle criteria pass but A fails and frozen evidence localizes the failed criteria to boundary/event formation. Otherwise select C or inconclusive exactly as above. Nonsignificance is not noninferiority. Report all baselines even if the branch is already determined. Do not manufacture success or relational superiority.

RESOURCES AND PUBLICATION

Existing per-assignment caps apply: <=1,000 total episode/control/invariance streams, <=2 hours aggregate local compute, <=2 GiB new artifacts, <=32 arrived chunks and <=2-second completed waveform units. Reserve held-out capacity before development and count every acoustic execution/probe; do not split work to evade caps. No spending, purchased/reset credits, limit increases, paid fallback, MERT change/download, foundation training or new paid dependency. If an actual limit blocks work, preserve recoverable progress and exact known reset/retry information, then exit without busy retrying.

Recheck live main, open PRs and any matching active work. Preserve processed-comment/version/assignment/SHA tracking and the no-overlap lock. Publish ONE complete successor with isolated code, frozen protocol, recipes/hashes, acoustic caches, pre-reveal logs, uncertainty/calibration, event and prediction results by group/control/model, source/execution provenance, checksums, concise report and updated `PROJECT_STATE.md`. Check sensitive files. New PR: draft → apply `earworm-review-ready` → ready, targeting main; update a matching ready PR only with a complete snapshot and label present. Link exact publication head, execution revision, outputs and successor PR back here. Save awaiting-review, release the lock and stop. No worker merge, force push, signal-only commit, duplicate worker/reviewer or schedule change.
